# BubblinCrude — audited state and backlog

Verified counts: **334 streams, 347 sites, 156 hubs, 696 refineries.**
Streams are clean — zero broken `related_ids`/`site_ids`/`hub_ids`, no duplicate
ids, yields sum to 100±10, TBP curves monotonic. Coverage: 100% api/sulfur/yields/
notes, 88% TAN, 63% distillation+resid, 61% metals, 5% SARA. `cuts` and `products`
are complete — do not "improve" them without a specific reason.

Never hand-edit the version; use `scripts/bump-version.py` and `--check`.

## 1. Refinery layer — capacity filled from Climate TRACE; keep matching conservative

600 of 696 have `capacity_kbd` (US from EIA-820, others from Climate TRACE v7
`oil-and-gas-refining`, CC BY 4.0). Rebuild via `scripts/build-refineries.py`.
Attaching a real capacity to the wrong plant is worse than leaving it null.
OSM junk (gas plants, sugar, chem, mining, South Pars, one-word company pins)
dropped; duplicate yards collapsed onto the pin that already had kb/d. EIA
company copied onto US `operator` (all **117** matched US plants — the 14 OSM
misses are now curated pins with published yards). 7 EIA rows stay skipped
(not crude CDUs / same yard). Named TRACE kb/d attached only when one pin and
one TRACE row agree (Jamnagar, Visakh, Thai Oil, Antwerp Total/Esso, Cubatão,
Paraguaná, Mina Al-Ahmadi, Kirishi, Basrah, SATORP Jubail). Operator filled
from a known company in the plant name when the name is more than that
company word.

Still open: 96 plants with no kb/d, 334 without `operator`, and **none** have
`related_ids`, so refineries still do not link to streams.

Honesty pass (v289): yield bins and TBP labeled vol% to match volume blend;
`S()` no longer flags a present value as unknown; four non-CDU pins dropped
(Nafoora field, Tazhong gathering station, Senegal/Mauritania “Old Refinery”,
inland SAMIR). Saved views renamed to the filter they actually apply.

Condensate kind (v290): **24** streams, all with an explicit `kind`. `S()` does
not infer it from the name or from API. Culzean, Belanak, and Terengganu added
because the records already called them condensate. One kind covers lease
condensate and plant pentanes-plus — EIA splits those; the glossary says so.
Kind is curated from production route. Check with `scripts/check-data.py`.

## 2. Field output and reserves — sites carry scale (v311)

167 site records have `production_kbd` / `condensate_kbd` / `reserves_mmbbl` /
`production_year` from GEM's Global Oil and Gas Extraction Tracker (March 2026,
CC BY 4.0). 134 have output, 123 reserves, out of 275 active fields in scope.
Rebuild with `scripts/build-volumes.py --goget <xlsx> --write`; the workbook is
registration-gated so it is never fetched. Crosswalk lives in
`scripts/site-goget-map.json`.

Matching needs name **and** distance to agree — proximity alone pairs Lula with
Lapa (7 km, different fields). `REJECT` drops three by hand (ek-banam/Balam,
changqing/Huaqing, christina-lake-site/Narrows Lake). `PARTIAL` flags four
boundary mismatches `estimated`. `nested_in` marks a site whose barrels sit
inside another matched unit (Guneshli in ACG, Mostarda and Gindungo in Kaombo)
so `siteRate()` returns 0 for it and nothing double-counts.

Crude and condensate stay separate — do not sum them. Pins are **not** sized by
output (deliberate: color already carries API/sulfur, and sizing would bury the
small grades); the `Field output` filter is the scale affordance instead, and it
shows on the sites layer only. A stream card totals its linked fields as
upstream context, never as that grade's export rate.

## 3. Pipelines — fifth layer, polylines not pins (v313)

`pipelines.js` (547 KB, ~125 KB gzipped, eagerly loaded and precached) holds
**1,093** crude trunk lines from GEM's Global Oil Infrastructure Tracker (June
2026, CC BY 4.0): oil only, operating or construction. 846 have design
capacity. Rebuild with `scripts/build-pipelines.py --xlsx … --geojson …`; both
downloads are registration-gated so nothing is fetched.

Routes are simplified to ~1 km, **1% of 2.6M source points**, stored as flat
`[lat,lon,lat,lon]` runs. Each record also carries a midpoint `lat`/`lon` so
search, fly-to, tooltips and compare reuse the pin code paths untouched — only
rendering is special. An invisible fat polyline under each line carries the
clicks (16 px touch, 10 px mouse); without it a 1.4 px stroke is untappable.

Capacity comes from GEM's `CapacityBOEd`, not `Capacity` — the latter is a
comma-formatted string and half the rows are mtpa. It is **design** throughput,
not flow, and shares one Compare bar with refinery capacity. `CAPACITY_SUSPECT`
drops P0809 Rotterdam-Venlo (recorded at 250 mtpa ≈ 5 mb/d, ~7× reality).
Regions are borrowed from the country assignments already in sites/hubs/
refineries, so pipelines speak the app's seven regions, not UN M49.

Checks that must keep holding: Trans-Alaska 2,136 kb/d / 1,288 km / 48 in /
1977, Petroline 5,000 kb/d.

Refactors this landed, do not re-fork them: `clearOtherSelections()` /
`otherSelectionsEmpty()` / `PIN_KIND_IDS` replace six copies of id-clearing;
`INSPECTOR_BY_KIND` replaces four copied dispatch blocks (a missing entry now
throws instead of falling through to the stream card); `layerHasAssay()`
replaces four hand-listed layer sets; `pickDefaultId(kind)` replaces four
pickDefault* functions.

## 4. Blend calculator — on Compare (v281)

Volume blend of ≥2 streams on the Compare board: SG-weighted gravity, mass-weighted
sulfur, volume-weighted yields and TBP (dashed mix line when every selected
stream has a curve). Honest limits in the card copy. Arab Light + Basrah Light
at half-and-half is the teaching check against Dubai. See `crude-blend-math`.

## 5. Phone filters — sheet on Compare-adjacent slider strip (v282)

Below 1100px the left rail is a bottom sheet. Open from the **Filter** end-cap
on the slider strip (same strip height; sliders lose width). Live apply, Done
closes. Kind / completeness / saved views are streams-only; sulfur class hides
on hubs and refineries. `#has-distill` now tests `distillation_curve` (211).
`sizeMapToBelt()` still sizes the map from width alone.

## 6. Marker clustering — skipped

Leave pins on true lat/lon. Clustering (and spiderfy) would hide or offset
dots at low zoom. If Europe tap collisions stay bad, disambiguate with a list
of what was under the finger — do not move markers.

