## Still open

Pipelines: 257 crude lines GEM tracks have no mapped route and are omitted
entirely; no `related_ids`, so a line does not link to the fields it drains or
the plants it feeds (its endpoints are place-name strings, not ids). NGL lines
(244 operating) and the GOIT product-pipeline set are unused. The tracker's
`Owner`/`Parent` chain is reduced to one owner name.

Sites: 92 active fields with no GEM match, 141 with no output figure. Streams
and hubs carry no volume at all — no grade export rate (not free at grade
level), no hub tank capacity (Cushing shell capacity *is* free from EIA weekly).
`ek-banam` is a misspelled id for Ek-Balam; renaming it would break `related_ids`.
Country labels still disagree across layers (sites say "United Arab Emirates",
streams say "UAE"; "Congo" vs "Republic of the Congo") — this silently breaks
cross-layer joins and cost a debugging pass during the volume build.

Refineries: 96 without kb/d, 334 without operator, zero `related_ids`.
US EIA holes closed (v287): 14 curated yards; 7 non-CDU/same-yard rows still skipped.
Aasta Hansteen stays Conventional (record calls it crude); do not auto-tag from API.
